{"id":1462,"date":"2020-11-27T20:06:03","date_gmt":"2020-11-28T04:06:03","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1462"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:38","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:38","slug":"program-trailer-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-trailer-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Program the Trailer Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216279c066\" name=\"6a2216279c066\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What it does<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The Trailer Bot can be controlled using a remote control. It can move forward or backward, curve to the right or left, and speed up or down.<\/p>\n<p>This is the Trailer Bot&#8217;s pseudocode with the remote control:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>If up is pressed, move forward.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if down is pressed, move backward.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if\u00a0right is pressed, curve right.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if\u00a0left is pressed, curve right.<\/li>\n<li>If F1 is pressed, speed up.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if\u00a0F2 is pressed, slow down.<\/li>\n<li>Otherwise, stop.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Fun thing about the Trailer Bot: you can use the LEDs to tell how fast (or slow) it&#8217;s going! If you turn on the four middle LEDs (13, 14, 15, and 16), an increase or decrease in the number of LEDs that are on shows an increase or decrease in the Trailer Bot&#8217;s speed.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216279c1a6\" name=\"6a2216279c1a6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Setup<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]There is a lot to include in the setup code! This is the breakdown:<\/p>\n<p>Before void setup():<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The Smart Inventor Library<\/li>\n<li>The speed variable<\/li>\n<li>The LED variables<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>In void setup():<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The motors<\/li>\n<li>The remote control<\/li>\n<li>The LEDs&#8217; output and state<\/li>\n<li>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint speed = 60;\r\n\r\nint speedMeterL = 13;\r\nint speedMeterR = 16;\r\nvoid setup() { \r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n    SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();\r\n\r\n     pinMode(11, OUTPUT); \/\/ set up the LEDs\r\n     pinMode(12, OUTPUT);\r\n     pinMode(13, OUTPUT);\r\n     pinMode(14, OUTPUT);\r\n     pinMode(15, OUTPUT);\r\n     pinMode(16, OUTPUT);\r\n     pinMode(17, OUTPUT);\r\n     pinMode(18, OUTPUT);\r\n\r\n     digitalWrite(13, HIGH);\r\n     digitalWrite(14, HIGH);\r\n     digitalWrite(15, HIGH);\r\n     digitalWrite(16, HIGH);\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216279c225\" name=\"6a2216279c225\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add remote control data<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Create a variable to read the remote control and store information about the last button that was pressed. You want this information to be read continuously, so make sure it&#8217;s in void loop().<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216279c283\" name=\"6a2216279c283\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add buttons<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next up is the exciting part of the code: telling your motors how to move! You need to bust out your if, else if, and else statements to program how your Trailer Bot will move if certain buttons on the remote control have been pressed. Again, because this should be continuously checked, this part of the code should be in the void loop() section.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n\r\n int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n\r\n  if(keyData == KEY_U)\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed); \/\/ Move forwards\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n }\r\n else if(keyData == KEY_D)\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed); \/\/ Move backwards\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n }\r\n else if(keyData == KEY_L)\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed); \/\/ Turn left\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n }\r\n else if(keyData == KEY_R)\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed); \/\/ Turn right\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n }\r\n else\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0); \/\/ Stop\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0);\r\n }\r\n\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216279c2de\" name=\"6a2216279c2de\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add F1 and F2<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]We&#8217;ve been telling you that your Trailer Bot can speed up or slow down, but you haven&#8217;t had the chance to program that part&#8230;until now! You can use the F1 and F2 buttons on the remote control to speed up or slow down the motors. Just like the buttons for directions, you need to use if and else if statements to do this.<\/p>\n<p>You also need to have your program check your Trailer Bot&#8217;s speed before it can go faster or slower. Make sure to include a short delay so you have time to let go of the button before the speed changes.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n\r\n int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n\r\n if(keyData == KEY_U)\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed); \/\/ Move forwards\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n }\r\n else if(keyData == KEY_D)\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed); \/\/ Move backwards\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n }\r\n else if(keyData == KEY_L)\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed); \/\/ Turn left\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n }\r\n else if(keyData == KEY_R)\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed); \/\/ Turn right\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n }\r\n else\r\n {\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0); \/\/ Stop\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0);\r\n }\r\n \r\n if(keyData == KEY_F1)\r\n {\r\n     if(speed &lt; 90) \/\/ make sure you are not going too fast\r\n         {\r\n             speed = speed + 20; \/\/ speed up\r\n             delay(150);\r\n         }\r\n }\r\n else if(keyData == KEY_F2)\r\n {\r\n     if(speed &gt; 30) \/\/ make sure you are not going too slow\r\n         {\r\n             speed = speed - 20; \/\/ slow down\r\n             delay(150);\r\n         }\r\n }\r\n\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216279c331\" name=\"6a2216279c331\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add LEDs<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]About those LEDs:\u00a0they can display how high or low\u00a0the current speed is. Each time the speed is increased or decreased, two more\u00a0LEDs should be turned on or off.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() { \r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData(); \r\n\r\n    if(keyData == KEY_U) { \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed); \/\/ Move forwards \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed); \r\n    } \r\n\r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_D) { \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed); \/\/ Move backwards \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed); \r\n    } \r\n\r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_L) { \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed); \/\/ Turn left \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed); \r\n    } \r\n\r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_R) { \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed); \/\/ Turn right \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed); \r\n    } \r\n    \r\n    else { SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0); \/\/ Stop \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0); \r\n    }  \r\n\r\n    if(keyData == KEY_F1) {     \r\n        if(speed &lt; 90) \/\/ make sure you are not going too fast         \r\n        {             \r\n            speed = speed + 20; \/\/ speed up\r\n\r\n            speedMeterL = speedMeterL - 1; \/\/light up two more LEDs\r\n            speedMeterR = speedMeterR + 1;\r\n\r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterL, HIGH);\r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterR, HIGH);\r\n             \r\n            delay(150);         \r\n        } \r\n       }\r\n     else if(keyData == KEY_F2) {     \r\n        if(speed &gt; 30) \/\/ make sure you are not going too slow         \r\n        {             \r\n            speed = speed - 20; \/\/ slow down\r\n\r\n            speedMeterL = speedMeterL + 1; \/\/turn off two outer LEDs\r\n            speedMeterR = speedMeterR - 1;\r\n\r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterL, LOW);\r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterR, LOW);\r\n \r\n            delay(150);         \r\n        }\r\n       }\r\n    }<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216279c384\" name=\"6a2216279c384\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This is what your final code should look like:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint speed = 60;\r\n\r\nint speedMeterL = 13;\r\nint speedMeterR = 16;\r\n\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {     \r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();    \r\n    SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();     \r\n\r\n    pinMode(11, OUTPUT); \/\/ set up the LEDs     \r\n    pinMode(12, OUTPUT);     \r\n    pinMode(13, OUTPUT);     \r\n    pinMode(14, OUTPUT);     \r\n    pinMode(15, OUTPUT);     \r\n    pinMode(16, OUTPUT);     \r\n    pinMode(17, OUTPUT);     \r\n    pinMode(18, OUTPUT);     \r\n\r\n    digitalWrite(13, HIGH);     \r\n    digitalWrite(14, HIGH);     \r\n    digitalWrite(15, HIGH);     \r\n    digitalWrite(16, HIGH);}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {     \r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();     \r\n\r\n    if(keyData == KEY_U) \r\n    {         \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed); \/\/ Move forwards         \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);     \r\n    }     \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_D) \r\n    {         \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed); \/\/ Move backwards         \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);     \r\n    }     \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_L) \r\n    {         \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed); \/\/ Turn left         \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);     \r\n    }     \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_R) \r\n    {         \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed); \/\/ Turn right         \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);     \r\n    }         \r\n    else \r\n    { \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0); \/\/ Stop         \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0);     \r\n    }      \r\n\r\n    if(keyData == KEY_F1) \r\n    {             \r\n        if(speed &lt; 90) \/\/ make sure you are not going too fast                 \r\n        {                         \r\n            speed = speed + 20; \/\/ speed up            \r\n\r\n            speedMeterL = speedMeterL - 1; \/\/light up two more LEDs            \r\n            speedMeterR = speedMeterR + 1;            \r\n\r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterL, HIGH);            \r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterR, HIGH);                         \r\n\r\n            delay(150);                 \r\n        }        \r\n    }     \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_F2) \r\n    {             \r\n        if(speed &gt; 30) \/\/ make sure you are not going too slow                 \r\n        {                         \r\n            speed = speed - 20; \/\/ slow down            \r\n\r\n            speedMeterL = speedMeterL + 1; \/\/turn off two outer LEDs            \r\n            speedMeterR = speedMeterR - 1;            \r\n\r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterL, LOW);            \r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterR, LOW);             \r\n\r\n            delay(150);                 \r\n        }       \r\n    }    \r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216279c3c7\" name=\"6a2216279c3c7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Not sure about the lesson or want to make sure you have the right code? Watch the video![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=cScqQ7KQ9wY&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 What it does [vc_column_text]The Trailer Bot can be controlled using a remote control. It can move forward or backward, curve to the right or left, and speed&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-trailer-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1736,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1760,1777,1808,1770,1793,1913,1915,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2163,2122,2171,2189,2190,2191],"class_list":["post-1462","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-sensors","lesson-tag-trailer","lesson-tag-trailer-bot","module-trailer","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1462","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1462\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1465,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1462\/revisions\/1465"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1736"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1462"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1462"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1462"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}